## 5. FEATURE DETAILS

### 5.1 Personal Branding (Brand Brain)

The brand profile is the foundation. Content generation requires >= 50% brand completeness (4 of 8 modules filled).

**8 Modules (guided AI chat for each):**

| Module | Key | What It Captures |
|--------|-----|-----------------|
| Foundation | `foundation` | Core identity, values, mission, origin story, expertise |
| ICA | `ica` | Target audience demographics, pain points, desires |
| Offer | `offer` | Product structure (MAGIC/Grand Slam framework), pricing |
| Brand Statement | `brand` | Positioning statement, unique mechanism, promise |
| Authority Building | `authority` | Credentials, social proof, case studies |
| Messaging | `messaging` | Key phrases, talking points, content themes, voice |
| Positioning | `positioning` | Market position, competitive angle, category design |
| Competitors | `competitors` | Competitor analysis, differentiation, white space |

**Multi-brand support:** One user can have multiple brand profiles. Brand selector in sidebar. Each brand has isolated chats, resources, content, memory.

**Brand Chat Flow:**
1. User goes to `/brands/[brandId]/chat/foundation`
2. AI coach asks guided questions from `MODULE_QUESTIONS`
3. User responds (text, voice mic, file upload, link, or resource picker)
4. Backend injects: module system prompt, writing style rules, resource context, performance data, agent memory, research context, file/link/picker attachments
5. AI responds with structured JSON (response + extracted data)
6. "Done, review form" extracts structured brand data into `profile_json`

### 5.2 Knowledge (Resource Library)

User's reference library. Everything the AI draws from for content generation.

**Sections:** My Story, Hooks, Titles, Scripts

**Input Methods:**
- Manual text entry
- File upload: PDF, DOCX, TXT, MD, CSV
- Image upload: PNG, JPG, GIF, WEBP (OCR via GPT-4 Vision)
- YouTube links (captions first, Whisper fallback)
- TikTok/Facebook video links (Whisper via yt-dlp)
- Reddit (post + top comments), Twitter/X (tweet + metrics)
- Substack articles, LinkedIn articles, any website (trafilatura)
- YouTube channel import (NotebookLM-style: imports all videos, extracts transcripts in background)

**Features:**
- Custom tags, Gold marking (high-priority for AI retrieval)
- Full-text + semantic search (pgvector embeddings)
- Re-extract transcripts for failed extractions
- Resource Picker: attach any resource to any chat in 1-2 clicks

### 5.3 Inspo Boards

Pinterest-style inspiration system. Multi-board with items that feed into the AI pipeline.

**Key Feature - Source Tagging with Intent:**
- **Source Tag:** Where it came from (auto-detected from URL)
- **Intent Note:** Why the user saved it and what the AI should learn from it

When attached to chat, the AI receives content + source tag + intent note as structured context.

### 5.4 Content Creation (Two Modes)

**Mode 1: Manual Chat (Canvas Workspace)**
- Route: `/content/chat`
- 3-panel layout: Left (chat history + settings), Middle (chat), Right (content editor/preview)
- AI generates content in markdown, right panel renders it
- Copy All, Export .md, section-by-section editing
- Settings: objective, type, platforms, tone, length, pillars

**Mode 2: Automation Pipeline (8-Node LangGraph)**
- Route: `/content/new` (create) -> `/content/[id]` (interact)
- Pipeline: `signal_research -> gap_analysis -> topic_selection (INTERRUPT) -> hook_lab (INTERRUPT) -> script_generation -> editor -> testing -> approval (INTERRUPT)`
- 3 interrupt points where user makes choices
- Each node injects: brand profile, knowledge, performance data, agent memory, experiments, voice DNA, live research
- Inline execution via `POST /workflows/{id}/execute` (Vercel-compatible, no worker needed)
- Frontend auto-executes on create and after each user interaction

**Content Settings:**
- Objective: Personal Branding, Sales, UGC, Ads, Entertainment
- Type: Educational, Storytelling, Opinion, How-to, News, Contrarian
- Platforms: YouTube, LinkedIn, Twitter/X, TikTok, Instagram
- Tone: Conversational, Professional, Authoritative, Casual, Bold, Inspirational
- Length: Short, Medium, Long, Extra Long
- Content Pillars: from brand profile

**Workflow Statuses:**
`queued` -> `running` -> `awaiting_topic` -> `awaiting_hook` -> `awaiting_approval` -> `completed`/`approved`/`rejected`/`failed`

### 5.5 Research Feed (TrendJacker-style)

- Route: `/research`
- Multi-platform feed: All, Reddit, LinkedIn, YouTube, TikTok
- Card grid layout with search bar, sort options (relevance, views, recent)
- Saved topic chips (session only)
- Backend aggregates from DuckDuckGo/Tavily, YouTube trends, Reddit, LinkedIn (via site: scoping), TikTok (via site: scoping)

### 5.6 Schedule

- Board view (Kanban: Draft -> Scheduled -> Published -> Archived)
- Calendar view (monthly/weekly)
- Import from completed workflows
- Export-only for MVP (no direct publishing yet)

### 5.7 Performance Tracker

4 tabs: Posts, Analytics, Voice DNA, Log Post

- Engagement rates, performance tiers (viral, strong, average, underperforming)
- Hook type breakdown (which hooks work)
- Voice DNA extraction from approved content
- Voice drift detection (is AI maintaining brand voice?)
- Performance data feeds back into content pipeline

### 5.8 Agent Brain (6 Cognitive Layers)

```
Layer 1: Memory (agent_memory.py) - observations, preferences, lessons, patterns
Layer 2: Performance (performance_analytics.py) - engagement rates, content patterns
Layer 3: Experiments (experiments.py) - A/B tests, auto-conclude with significance
Layer 4: Voice Identity (self_voice.py + voice_analysis.py) - voice DNA, drift detection
Layer 5: Content Pipeline (worker/graph/nodes/) - 8-node LangGraph with checkpoints
Layer 6: Live Research (web_search.py + research.py) - DuckDuckGo, YouTube, Reddit
```

**Compound Learning Loop:**
```
Content Created -> Published -> Performance Tracked -> Patterns Detected
     ^                                                        |
     |                                                        v
     +---- Agent Memory Updated ---- Experiments Proposed ----+
     |                                                        |
     +---- Voice DNA Refined ------- Pipeline Improved -------+
```

### 5.9 Usage Tracking

- LLM token usage per workflow step
- Estimated cost per workflow
- Daily/monthly usage totals
- Per-user daily caps (configurable)
- Cost breakdown by model

### 5.10 Export Options

From completed workflows:
- Copy to clipboard
- Download as .md
- Google Docs export (requires OAuth setup)
- Notion export (requires OAuth setup)
- Import to Schedule

